# The sources a release's worker images are built from. .github/workflows/release.yml (and radiance-image.yml) read
# this file; change it in a reviewed commit before tagging, never in a workflow run. All three are public: the
# workflows clone them anonymously at these commits (tools/release.py pins checks the format).
#
# rad-exl3-mix: the quantizer paths docker/build.sh copies (quantize/ourq.py, the exllamav3 patch series, the side
# extensions, the staged golden recorder). Its commit enters ourq's code stamp: pin the commit the ladder is quantized
# with.
RXM_REPO_URL=https://github.com/TheHeroBrine422/rad-exl3-mix
RXM_COMMIT=37ac169c0e30f206b1232f6e5b72a1c35a0ec3b7
# radiance (eval_mix, golden_record): our fork, branch qc-exl3-v3, on Codeberg. Its image is built and published on
# its own (radiance-image.yml: a patched LLVM and a ROCm base, hours and tens of GB, so not in every release) and
# pinned here by digest: ghcr.io/theherobrine422/rad-quant-at-home-radiance@sha256:<64 hex>. Empty: the ROCm release
# build stops and says so (the CUDA image does not use it).
RADIANCE_REPO_URL=https://codeberg.org/Hero422/radiance
RADIANCE_COMMIT=42960d54dd8ad9c7ca4a3d28a9e2179da1f8faee
RADIANCE_IMAGE=
